/* ==================================================================
   Central Automation - Estimate and Quotation
   07. Import the CA project list into the register (GENERATED: do not edit by hand)

   Source      CA_Projects_List_As_of_July_2026.xlsx (190 projects)
   Generated   by database\tools\generate_ca_projects_import.js, which costs every project with the
               estimator's own calculation (the same figures the page registers on submit).
   Result      each project becomes a VERIFIED entry (dbo.SwProjectRegister) with a "submit" and a
               "verify" row in dbo.SwProjectLog, costed with the estimator's default masters (rates and prices in estimator.js).
   Safe to run again: a project whose RegisterId already exists is skipped, never changed.

   The workbook has almost no cost data, so these ASSUMPTIONS were used for every project:
     Team        1 person: Senior for AI / ML / vision / digital twin / mathematical model, else Mid
                 (3 people where the sheet says FTE 3: BF Alkali Model, BF Liquid Levels Height Prediction)
     Duration    working days (Mon-Fri) from Start to End date; "till date" = 31 Jul 2026,
                 "till next year" = 31 Mar 2027; a missing date = 90 days
     Complexity  Very high: AI / ML / vision / digital twin; High: mathematical model, rule-base model; else Standard
     Sizing      100 users, 1 server (8 cores, 32 GB, 2 TB SSD), SQL Server Standard, Windows Server,
                 yearly delivery model, 3 years of ownership, default loadings and AMC
     Value       "Cal-2 (Gained)" amounts are a yearly benefit (other benefit, INR); other projects: none
     Dates       financial year from the Start Date (else End Date, else 2026-27)
   Edit @ImportUser below if the entries should belong to someone else.

   These entries are ESTIMATES (every Note starts "Estimated from the project list") but are stored as verified, so reports count them.
   A verified entry cannot be edited or deleted on the page. To undo this import (the log rows go with the entries):
       DELETE dbo.SwProjectRegister WHERE SubmittedBy = N'Import';
   Registering one of these projects again on the page creates a second row for it (a different RegisterId); delete the imported row first.
   ================================================================== */

